.TH S3FS-EBPF 1 "" "s3fs-ebpf" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
s3fs-ebpf \- S3 file system with an eBPF-driven page cache
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B s3fs-ebpf
.I command
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B s3fs-ebpf
mounts an S3-compatible bucket through the in-kernel
.B s3fs_ebpf
VFS (the
.B s3fs_kfunc
kernel module).
The daemon serves read misses, flushes and syncs to the object store, and attaches the cache policy (CEL, or an eBPF struct_ops program) that decides what the page cache keeps.
.PP
The kernel module must match the running kernel exactly.
Install the
.BI s3fs-ebpf-kmod- kernel-release
package for
.BR "uname -r" .
.SH COMMANDS
Each command has its own manual page,
.BR s3fs-ebpf-\fIcommand\fR (1).
.TP
.B mount
Mount an S3 bucket via the s3fs_ebpf VFS.
.TP
.B unmount
Unmount a previously mounted target.
.TP
.B fastpath
Run the fastpath daemon: attach fentry/vfs_getattr, serve read misses, flush, sync S3.
.TP
.B stats
Print fast/slow path counters.
.TP
.B policy
Hot-reload the cache policy blob.
.TP
.B hash-policy
Print the SHA256 of a user policy .bpf.o, for allowlist entries.
.TP
.B s3-list
List objects in a bucket (\fB\-\-backend\fR s3|gcs).
.TP
.B s3-stat
Stat a single object (\fB\-\-backend\fR s3|gcs).
.TP
.B dev
Development, probe and demo commands.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B S3FS_EBPF_ROOT
Directory that holds
.IR bpf/ ,
where built-in policies (\fB\-\-policy\-bpf builtin:\fIname\fR) are looked up.
Default: the current directory or its parent when it has a
.I bpf
subdirectory, else
.IR /usr/share/s3fs-ebpf .
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /usr/share/s3fs-ebpf/bpf/*.bpf.o
Built-in eBPF cache policies.
.TP
.I /usr/share/s3fs-ebpf/policies/
Example CEL policies and the allowlist example.
.TP
.I /lib/modules/KERNEL/updates/s3fs_kfunc.ko
The kernel module, one package per kernel release.
.TP
.I /usr/share/doc/s3fs-ebpf-doc/
Full documentation (package
.BR s3fs-ebpf-doc ).
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR s3fs-ebpf-fastpath (1),
.BR s3fs-ebpf-mount (1),
.BR modprobe (8),
.BR depmod (8)
